<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH PVT CZK 52.3 MLN 9MO GROSS PROFIT.</title>
<headline>CZECH PVT CZK 52.3 MLN 9MO GROSS PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine-month period</p>
<p>ending September 30, 1996 (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit		 52.3    vs    649.7</p>
<p> Operational profit	 51.0    vs    648.99</p>
<p> Sales from services     957.0    vs  1,518.6</p>
<p> Assets		    2,086.1    vs  2,160.7</p>
<p> Basic capital	     784.0    vs  784.0</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is PVT a.s., a computer network</p>
<p>firm. Results were supplied directly by the company. PVT shares</p>
<p>are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Company officials and analysts have said a sharp drop in</p>
<p>the firm's results was expected since 1995 figures reflect the</p>
<p>company's involvement in the second wave of the government's</p>
<p>massive privatisation programme.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
